.nh
.TH "PB-ENV-LIST" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-list - List configured environment-variable metadata


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List configured environment-variable metadata

.PP
List ENV names and scope metadata, optionally limited to a team or host. This does not print plaintext values or key material.

.PP
ENV values are encrypted before they leave the client. Commands select personal, team, or host scope explicitly; list output shows metadata rather than secret values. Unlock the local vault when a key operation requires it.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print redacted JSON metadata

.PP
\fB--machine\fP=""
	machine name or ID; defaults to the personal scope

.PP
\fB--team\fP=""
	team scope; defaults to this account's personal scope


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env(1)\fP
